config COMPONENTS_TFLM_ENABLE
    bool "Enable TFLM (TensorFlow Lite for Microcontrollers)"
    default n
    help
      Enable TensorFlow Lite for Microcontrollers, so that customer-supplied
      .tflite models can run on the CPU.

      This is independent of the .inm NPU path in components/ai: the NPU
      yields the core while it computes, so a TFLM model and a .inm model can
      run concurrently on IPRO7. TFLM cannot drive the NPU itself - the NPU
      consumes an offline-compiled instruction stream and TFLM has no delegate
      mechanism. License: Apache 2.0.

if COMPONENTS_TFLM_ENABLE

config TFLM_NMSIS_NN_KERNELS
    bool "Use NMSIS-NN optimized kernels"
    default y
    select COMPONENTS_NMSIS_NN_ENABLE
    help
      Replace 14 reference kernels (conv, depthwise_conv, fully_connected,
      pooling, softmax, svdf, lstm, ...) with the NMSIS-NN backend, which uses
      the RISC-V P-extension when the app is built with an xxldsp march.

      Costs flash - the SIMD kernels are several times larger than the
      reference ones - and buys speed. Turn off to measure the difference or
      when flash is tight.

config TFLM_SIGNAL_OPS
    bool "Include signal processing ops (FFT, filter bank)"
    default n
    help
      Audio front-end operators used by micro_speech style models. Pulls in
      kissfft. Leave off for vision-only models.

config TFLM_STRIP_ERROR_STRINGS
    bool "Strip error strings"
    default n
    help
      Compile out human-readable error messages to save flash. Debugging a
      model that fails to allocate gets considerably harder - keep this off
      during bring-up.

endif
